From be3cf8081d78ca212e82d7002d0e2e7237c450dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:57:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): order operator releases by portable event time
 [daveey]

Copied-in older shared-wall assertions receive larger local row ids and were
revoking newer operator unblocks. Compare UUIDv7 millisecond clocks (legacy
created_at fallback), with local ids only breaking exact ties. Extract the
existing fence decoder rather than creating another UUID parser.

Share the guard's read-only hold evaluator with CLI and tool unblock reporting.
Name the running sibling or probe interval due in PT; preserve registered-wall
own-card and unregistered-wall sibling precedence and the public guard contract.

Proof: RED had 10 behavioral failures. GREEN shared-blockers plus all #2923
files: 160 tests pass. Consumer run: 427 tests pass across 14 files (before
adding two more clock-selection cases). scripts/check: 20 checks pass.
Three killed mutants: id-only ordering, omitted id tie-break, ignored UUID.
Read-only local board replay found no remaining open blockers, so that is not
live unblock proof; deployed worker proof remains a post-land acceptance step.
